# Exemplars are YOUR real documents - finished reports, proposals, file notes,
# the ones you would hand a new starter. This repo is public, so nothing here is
# committed: every file is ignored except the README that documents what belongs
# in the folder.
#
# That is also what makes the folder itself committable. Git stores no empty
# directories, so this folder survives in the repo because of its README, and
# the skill installs with somewhere to put your exemplars already in place.
#
# Drop your files in here, then copy the whole skill folder to your endpoint:
#     Copy-Item -Recurse -Force .\skills\exemplar-writer "$env:USERPROFILE\.claude\skills"
#
# To commit one deliberately (a genuinely generic, de-identified example):
#     git add -f skills/exemplar-writer/exemplars/"Status Report - Example.md"

*
!*/
!README.md
!.gitignore
